AltoCappedChainlinkOracle::constructor()
├── given invalid inputs
│   ├── when owner is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with OwnableInvalidOwner
│   ├── when chainlink node feed is zero address
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleChainlinkInvalidInput
│   ├── when chainlink node stalePeriod is zero
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleChainlinkInvalidInput
│   ├── when chainlink node inDecimals + outDecimals is greater than 54
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleChainlinkInvalidInput
│   ├── when chainlink node feedDecimals does not match feed decimals
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleChainlinkInvalidInput
│   ├── when ERC4626 ratio node initialRatio is zero
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleERC4626RatioInvalidInput
│   ├── when ERC4626 ratio node initialTimestamp is greater than block.timestamp
│   │   └── it should revert with ModuleERC4626RatioInvalidInput
│   └── when ERC4626 ratio node maxYearlyGrowthRatioWad is zero
│       └── it should revert with ModuleERC4626RatioInvalidInput
└── given valid inputs
    ├── it should set owner correctly
    ├── it should set chainlinkNode correctly
    ├── it should set erc4626RatioNode correctly
    ├── it should emit SetChainlinkNode with zero-value old node and new node
    └── it should emit SetERC4626RatioNode with zero-value old node and new node
